    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88386" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προπρηνής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
		stronger form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρηνής,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with the face downwards,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν κόνι ἐκτανύσας προπρηνέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.18
				</span></i>
			; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φασγάνῳ] προπρηνέϊ</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προπρηνέα</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> τύψας</span>
			<i>with the edge of</i> the sword, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.98
			</span></i>: neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προπρηνές</span> as
				Adv., <i>forward,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπίσω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.218
			</span></i>. [<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always makes first syll. long.]</div>
